<h1>Church Management Software</h1>

<p class="lead">Church management software that brings congregation, volunteers, events, and giving into one place — so pastors and volunteer leaders aren’t juggling four tools and a group chat.</p>

<img src="/images/ss-directory.png" alt="Church directory showing families, small groups, and volunteer teams" width="826" height="826" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;" class="rounded border">

<section id="why-church" class="card" aria-labelledby="why-church-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="why-church-heading">A quiet backbone for busy congregations</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Churches keep track of people, not just members — families, small groups, volunteer teams, and seasonal events. GatherPack gives each person one record (relationships like parent/child, contact info, notes) and lets teams scope what they see. Small-group leaders manage their group’s events and attendance; the office keeps the whole view. No more reply-all or “only one person knows” spreadsheets.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Open source under the <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a>: self-host free for full control, or <a href="/hosting/">managed hosting</a> via Sledgehammer Infosystems if you’d rather not run servers. <a href="/open-source/">Compare options</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="tailored" class="card" aria-labelledby="tailored-heading">
